      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `InterpolatorStringLookup` correctly routes a key with an empty prefix (e.g., `\":\"` followed by text) to the `XmlEncoderStringLookup` registered under the empty-string key, which XML-encodes the apostrophe. I'll improve readability with better names, remove unused imports, and add an explanatory comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes unused imports, renames variables to be more descriptive (`lookupMap`, `xmlEncoderLookup`, `interpolator`, `result`), and adds a method-level Javadoc plus inline comments explaining the prefix-routing logic and XML encoding behavior — all without changing the called methods, arguments, or expected outcomes."
    }
